\f1\fs22 \'93Shut up, Alexander.\'94\
That was Eloise.\
Hayley kept her gun on Alexander as Sarah negotiated Eloise backstage.\
A shadowy Kathy met them at the curtain. \'93Are you all right?\'94 she asked Sarah as she relieved her of pushing Eloise\'92s chair.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \'93I\'92m standing up, aren\'92t I?\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf2 The office chair wheels kept jamming on cables and bumping into obstacles.\
\'93Tax!\'94 Eloise swore as Kathy bunted her into  a crate. \'93What is this? An amusement chair ride? Someone give me their device.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Sarah handed hers over. Eloise switched on the light and pointed it at her shoes to see how badly her shoe tips had been damaged.\
A second light found them. Eloise returned the beam and trapped a woman wearing a headset in it. Her eyes were large behind multifocals and her mouth was agape.\
\'93Do something!\'94 Alexander ordered his stage manager. \'93Get lighting and a camera. Use your tablet if you have to.\'94\
The stage manager disappeared like a threatened bandicoot.\
\'93You\'92re a genius, Hayleykins! The ratings will be through the roof. I\'92m not sure what you have planned next. I\'92m happy to offer notes.\'94\
\'93Shut up, Alexander.\'94\
That was still Eloise. \'93And someone get me out of this chair.\'94\
\'93Wait till I\'92ve got a camera rolling,\'94 Alexander directed.\
\'93Shut up, Alexander.\'94\
That was Sarah and Hayley.\
And Eloise.\
Kathy felt a little sorry for him.\
Chip stepped into the light ahead of them.\
Alexander brightened. \'93Mr Stockwell. How did you like your segment?\'94\
Chip looked to Eloise. She read the message: 
\f2\i Can I just strangle him right now?\

\f1\i0 A beam of light and the outline of a man approached them quickly. \'93Ms Shakti! Ms Shakti! Oh, thank Murugan!\'94\
Bala Chuglingham advanced on them. Light caught a box-cutter in his hand.\
Eloise flinched.\
So did Alexander, thinking he was about to get his throat cut, and fearing he might have his face disfigured as well.\
Bala arrested his haste. \'93I am freeing you from your chair,\'94 he explained.\
Alexander objected. \'93Wait for a camera!\'94\
\'93Shut up, Alexander.\'94 \
Eloise nodded, and Bala set to cutting the tape binding Eloise\'92s arms. \'93I cut the power. You have been so good to me and my family, Ms Shakti. I could not abide having sharks feeding on you.\'94\
Chip felt a flush of guilt.\
Once freed, Eloise pushed Bala back to get to her feet.\
Bala folded the loose tape into a sticky ball and tossed it aside. \'93Follow me,\'94 Bala said, holding up his security pass. \'93Maintenance workers have all the best access.\'94 His teeth were the brightest things back stage when he smiled. \'93Follow me.\'94\
Alexander reached for his suit pocket. Hayley nudged the back of his head with her gun muzzle.\
\'93If we\'92re not waiting for a proper crew, then I should film this.\'94\
\'93No.\'94\
\'93Think of the ratings. I\'92ll give you an executive producer credit.\'94\
\'93You give your hair stylists executive producer credits.\'94\
Alexander shrugged. \'93They produce my hair,\'94 he argued.\
Bala pocketed the boxcutter. \'93Come.\'94\
He led them between flight cases and a rack of costumes to a backstage stairwell. A small light on his maintenance device showed the steps.\
\'93How far down?\'94 Kathy asked.\
\'93Sub-basement.\'94\
She turned to Sarah. \'93Take your time.\'94\
From the auditorium came a burst of shouting.\
\'93Within reason,\'94 Hayley added.\
Eloise started down behind Bala. Sarah followed with one hand on the rail and Kathy close beside her. Alexander looked back for his crew.\
\'93Down,\'94 Hayley directed.\
Chip came at the rear, feeling clumsy in the stairwell.\
At the first stairwell landing Sarah stopped, shifted her weight and waited. \'93Keep going,\'94 she said. \'93You\'92re all making it worse.\'94\
At the bottom, Bala approached a plain door and presented his maintenance pass. The lock clicked.\
Beyond it was a service tunnel. Bala held the door while they went through, then pulled it shut and checked the handle.\
\'93This connects to the office park,\'94 he said.\
Eloise looked along the tunnel. \'93It does. I presume you know how to get to the Traverse station without attracting attention.\'94\
Sarah leaned against the wall and Kathy rested a hand on her back while Bala detailed the route; Eloise nodded approval.\
\'93And then?\'94 Hayley asked.\
\'93The research levels. Bunker accommodation. Situation rooms.\'94 Eloise rubbed the last adhesive from her wrist. \'93Very defendable.\'94\
\'93Against your own security?\'94 Hayley asked.\
\'93I\'92ll convince them to stand down,\'94 Alexander offered. \'93Tell them how they made the show such a success, offer to do follow-up interviews with them.\'94\
Hayley exchanged glances with Chip and Eloise.\
\'93That, and I still have a few tricks in my hand bag,\'94 Eloise said.
